  <text>
    <status value="extensions"/><div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><p class="res-header-id"><b>Generated Narrative: ValueSet ahip-religion-spirituality</b></p><a name="ahip-religion-spirituality"> </a><a name="hcahip-religion-spirituality"> </a><p>This value set includes codes based on the following rules:</p><ul><li>Include these codes as defined in <a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html"><code>http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-ReligiousAffiliation</code></a><span title="Version is explicitly stated to be 4.0.0"> version &#x1F4CD;4.0.0</span><table class="none"><tr><td style="white-space:nowrap"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1006">1006</a></td><td>Animism</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1004">1004</a></td><td>Agnostic (not sure if there is a God)</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1007">1007</a></td><td>Atheist (do not believe in God)</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1008">1008</a></td><td>Baha'I</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1043">1043</a></td><td>Church of Scientology</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1014">1014</a></td><td>Confucianism</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1020">1020</a></td><td>Hinduism</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1021">1021</a></td><td>Humanism</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1023">1023</a></td><td>Islam, Nation of Islam (Muslim)</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1025">1025</a></td><td>Jehovah's Witnesses</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1026">1026</a></td><td>Judaism (Jewish)</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1027">1027</a></td><td>Mormonism (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints/LDS)</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1037">1037</a></td><td>Paganism</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1044">1044</a></td><td>Shamanism</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1047">1047</a></td><td>Sikhism</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1050">1050</a></td><td>Taoism</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1052">1052</a></td><td>Unitarian Universalist</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1056">1056</a></td><td>VooDoo</td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-ReligiousAffiliation.html#v3-ReligiousAffiliation-1060">1060</a></td><td>Zoroastrianism</td></tr></table></li><li>Include these codes as defined in <a href="CodeSystem-ahip-demo-temporary-codes.html"><code>http://hl7.org/fhir/us/demographic-collect/CodeSystem/ahip-demo-temporary-codes</code></a><span title="Version is not explicitly stated, which means it is fixed to the version provided in this specification"> version &#x1F4E6;0.1.0</span><table class="none"><tr><td style="white-space:nowrap"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td><a href="CodeSystem-ahip-demo-temporary-codes.html#ahip-demo-temporary-codes-BUDD">BUDD</a></td><td>Buddhism</td><td>The religious and philosophical traditions based on the teachings of the Buddha</td></tr><tr><td><a href="CodeSystem-ahip-demo-temporary-codes.html#ahip-demo-temporary-codes-CHRI">CHRI</a></td><td>Christianity (e.g. Protestant, Roman Catholic, Russian Orthodox, Seventh-day Adventist)</td><td>Catholic, Protestant, Orthodox, and other Christian denominations</td></tr><tr><td><a href="CodeSystem-ahip-demo-temporary-codes.html#ahip-demo-temporary-codes-OBEA">OBEA</a></td><td>Obeahism</td><td>System of beliefs and practices found primarily in the former British colonies of the Caribbean</td></tr><tr><td><a href="CodeSystem-ahip-demo-temporary-codes.html#ahip-demo-temporary-codes-SBNR">SBNR</a></td><td>Spiritual but not religious</td><td>A term used to describe people who have a spiritual philosophy but do not adhere to any particular religious tradition</td></tr></table></li><li>Include these codes as defined in <a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-NullFlavor.html"><code>http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/v3-NullFlavor</code></a><span title="Version is explicitly stated to be 4.0.0"> version &#x1F4CD;4.0.0</span><table class="none"><tr><td style="white-space:nowrap"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td><a href="http://terminology.hl7.org/7.4.0/CodeSystem-v3-NullFlavor.html#v3-NullFlavor-ASKU">ASKU</a></td><td>I don't know</td><td>Information was sought but not found (e.g., patient was asked but didn't know)</td></tr></table></li><li>Include these codes as defined in <a href="CodeSystem-ahip-demo-additional-nullFlavor.html"><code>http://hl7.org/fhir/us/demographic-collect/CodeSystem/ahip-demo-additional-nullFlavor</code></a><span title="Version is not explicitly stated, which means it is fixed to the version provided in this specification"> version &#x1F4E6;0.1.0</span><table class="none"><tr><td style="white-space:nowrap"><b>Code</b></td><td><b>Display</b></td><td><b>Definition</b></td></tr><tr><td><a href="CodeSystem-ahip-demo-additional-nullFlavor.html#ahip-demo-additional-nullFlavor-CNTR">CNTR</a></td><td>I choose not to respond at this time</td><td>This code is to represent explicitly that the patient has chosen not to respond to this question at this time.</td></tr></table></li></ul></div>
